# Copy this file's variable NAMES into Vercel → your Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. Never commit a real .env file with real values to
# GitHub — this .env.example file (with no real values) is safe to commit.

# From Cashfree Dashboard → Developers → API Keys.
# This IS sent to the browser (indirectly, as part of deciding which
# Cashfree JS SDK mode to load) via the "environment" value returned by
# /api/create-order — but the App ID itself is only ever used server-side
# in this project's code. Keep it out of index.html regardless.
CASHFREE_APP_ID=

# From the same screen. NEVER put this in index.html or any frontend file.
# Server-side environment variable only, read only by lib/cashfree.js.
# Also used to verify webhook signatures — Cashfree does not require a
# separate, self-invented webhook secret the way some other gateways do.
CASHFREE_SECRET_KEY=

# "sandbox" while testing (fake payments, no real money), "production" once
# KYC is approved and you're ready for real ₹96 payments. Defaults to
# "sandbox" if left unset — set this explicitly before going live.
CASHFREE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# Added automatically when you attach the "Redis on Vercel" (Upstash)
# storage integration to this project — you will not type these in by
# hand, Vercel fills them in for you. Listed here just so you recognize
# them if you see them in the Vercel dashboard.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
